.TH YAZSES 1 "2026-08-07" "yazses 2.15.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yazses \- Local, offline voice dictation \(em hold a key, speak, release.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yazses
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS\fR]... [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Local, offline voice dictation \(em hold a key, speak, release.
Hold a key anywhere on the desktop, speak, release it, and the transcribed text is injected into whatever application is focused. Runs fully offline after the initial model download.
.SH COMMANDS
The complete command tree. For grouped, example-rich help run \fByazses \-\-help\fR or \fByazses \fICOMMAND\fR \-\-help\fR.
.SS "yazses about"
Show author, version, links, and where to report issues or request features.
.SS "yazses acronyms"
Manage a persistent acronym glossary and expand acronyms in text \(em offline.
.TP
\fByazses acronyms add\fR \fIACRONYM\fR \fIFULL\fR
Register an acronym \(-> full-form expansion in your glossary.
.TP
\fByazses acronyms expand\fR \fITEXT\fR
Expand known acronyms on first use ('Full Name (ACR)'), contract after \(em offline.
.TP
\fByazses acronyms list\fR
Show your stored acronym glossary.
.TP
\fByazses acronyms remove\fR \fIACRONYM\fR
Remove an acronym from your glossary.
.SS "yazses audio"
See and pin the input microphone (fixes a mic that silently switches).
.TP
\fByazses audio devices\fR
List capture-capable audio input devices.
.TP
\fByazses audio status\fR
Show the pinned mic, the OS default, and (if running) live capture health.
.TP
\fByazses audio use\fR \fINAME\fR
Pin the input microphone by name so a monitor/headset can't steal capture.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-clear\fR
Unpin; follow the OS default.
.RE
.SS "yazses autostart"
Start YazSes automatically at login, so it survives a reboot.
.TP
\fByazses autostart disable\fR
Stop starting YazSes at login. The daemon keeps running until you stop it.
.TP
\fByazses autostart enable\fR
Install and enable the login service, so YazSes is running when you sit down.
.TP
\fByazses autostart status\fR
Say whether YazSes will be running after the next reboot.
.SS "yazses braille"
Translate text to Unicode Braille (UEB subset) \(em fully offline.
.br
Arguments: \fItext\fR
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-grade\fR
UEB grade: 1 (uncontracted) or 2 (contracted).
.RE
.SS "yazses case"
Recase text to a naming convention \(em fully offline.
.br
Arguments: \fItext\fR
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-style\fR
Target case: snake|kebab|camel|pascal|title|sentence|upper|lower|constant. Omit to detect a spoken 'make this \&... case' command in the text.
.RE
.SS "yazses chords"
Turn a spoken key chord into injectable key combos \(em fully offline.
.br
Arguments: \fItext\fR
.SS "yazses cite"
Resolve a spoken 'author year' reference against a .bib file \(em fully offline.
.br
Arguments: \fIquery\fR
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-bib\fR
Path to a BibTeX (.bib) file.
.TP
\fB\-\-style\fR
latex | plain | apa.
.RE
.SS "yazses cliphistory"
A persistent clipboard history you can recall by voice-style reference \(em offline.
.TP
\fByazses cliphistory add\fR \fITEXT\fR
Add an entry to your clipboard history (newest first, de-duplicated, capped).
.TP
\fByazses cliphistory list\fR
Show your clipboard history, newest first.
.TP
\fByazses cliphistory recall\fR \fIQUERY\fR
Print the history entry a spoken reference points to \(em offline.
.SS "yazses coach"
Show private speaking-style analytics (filler rate, words-per-minute, vocabulary).
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-limit, \-n\fR
How many recent dictations to analyse.
.RE
.SS "yazses corpus"
Inspect or clear the local learning corpus.
.TP
\fByazses corpus destroy\fR
Irreversibly delete the entire learning corpus (database + audio clips).
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-i\-mean\-it\fR
Required: confirm irreversible wipe.
.RE
.TP
\fByazses corpus forget\fR
Delete recently captured events (e.g. after dictating something private).
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-minutes, \-m\fR
Delete events from the last N minutes.
.RE
.TP
\fByazses corpus status\fR
Show the learning corpus size, event counts, and date range.
.SS "yazses doctor"
Check system prerequisites and report what's OK / missing.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-mic\fR
Also record a short ambient clip and compare its level to the VAD threshold.
.RE
.SS "yazses enroll"
Run the accessibility enrollment wizard to calibrate VAD thresholds.
.SS "yazses enroll-voice"
Record a short voiceprint so YazSes can recognise your voice.
.SS "yazses features"
See capabilities and turn them on/off (no config-editing needed).
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-on\fR
Show only capabilities that are currently ON.
.TP
\fB\-\-tier\fR
Filter by advice tier: core, on, rec, opt, exp.
.TP
\fB\-\-category, \-c\fR
Filter by category name (partial, case-insensitive), e.g. 'access'.
.RE
.TP
\fByazses features disable\fR \fINAME\fR
Turn a capability OFF (writes your config), then `yazses restart` to apply.
.TP
\fByazses features enable\fR \fINAME\fR
Turn a capability ON (writes your config), then `yazses restart` to apply.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Allow enabling experimental features.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-install\fR
Don't auto-install the feature's optional deps.
.RE
.TP
\fByazses features info\fR \fINAME\fR
Describe a capability \(em what it does, a usage example, and how to toggle it.
.SS "yazses findreplace"
Apply a spoken find-and-replace to text \(em fully offline.
.br
Arguments: \fIcommand\fR
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-in\fR
Text to apply it to (omit to read stdin).
.RE
.SS "yazses gaze"
Aim dictation with your gaze \(em type into whichever pane you look at.
.TP
\fByazses gaze calibrate\fR
Calibrate the webcam so your gaze maps to screen zones.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-install\fR
Don't auto-install the gaze deps (mediapipe, opencv).
.RE
.TP
\fByazses gaze status\fR
Show whether look-to-pane is ready: deps, desktop backend, calibration.
.SS "yazses gitvoice"
Turn a spoken git command into a git command \(em fully offline.
.br
Arguments: \fItext\fR
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-run\fR
Run the command instead of only printing it.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Confirm a destructive command so --run will run it.
.RE
.SS "yazses hotkey"
Change the key you hold to talk.
.TP
\fByazses hotkey command\fR \fIKEY\fR
Set a dedicated *command* key, then `yazses restart` to apply.
.TP
\fByazses hotkey set\fR \fIKEY\fR
Set the key you hold to dictate, then `yazses restart` to apply.
.TP
\fByazses hotkey show\fR
Show the current hold-to-talk key (and command key, if set).
.SS "yazses inject"
Type text into the focused window without recording (tests the injector).
.br
Arguments: \fItext\fR
.SS "yazses logs"
Show the daemon's diagnostic log (metadata only -- no dictated text).
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-lines, \-n\fR
Number of recent lines to show.
.TP
\fB\-\-path\fR
Print the log file path and exit.
.RE
.SS "yazses mark-wrong"
Flag the last dictation as a misrecognition (a learning signal).
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-correction, \-c\fR
What you actually said (optional).
.RE
.SS "yazses meeting"
Hands-free meeting recording with who-said-what speaker labels + notes.
.TP
\fByazses meeting enroll\fR \fIMEETING_ID\fR
Enroll a meeting speaker as a named voiceprint so they're auto-named next time.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-speaker\fR
Cluster id to enroll, e.g. speaker_1.
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR
The person's name, e.g. Alice.
.RE
.TP
\fByazses meeting list\fR
List stored meetings on this machine (no daemon required).
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print meetings as a JSON array (machine-readable; empty list is []).
.RE
.TP
\fByazses meeting notes\fR \fIMEETING_ID\fR
Generate meeting minutes (summary, decisions, action items) from the transcript.
.TP
\fByazses meeting relabel\fR \fIMEETING_ID\fR
Fix speaker labels \(em merge two clusters and/or rename them \(em and re-render.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-merge\fR
Fold one speaker into another: SPEAKER_2=speaker_1 (repeatable).
.TP
\fB\-\-rename\fR
Name a speaker: speaker_1=Alice (repeatable).
.TP
\fB\-\-format, \-f\fR
Transcript format to re-render.
.RE
.TP
\fByazses meeting start\fR
Start recording a meeting (hands-free \(em no key to hold).
.TP
\fByazses meeting status\fR
Show the running meeting (elapsed + live transcript) or recent meetings.
.TP
\fByazses meeting stop\fR
Stop the recording and generate the speaker-labelled transcript (and notes).
.SS "yazses mic-level"
Measure mic speech level and recommend (or set) the VAD threshold.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-seconds, \-s\fR
Seconds to record while you speak.
.TP
\fB\-\-set\fR
Write the recommended vad_threshold to config.
.RE
.SS "yazses model"
Manage SLM intent-routing models (download / list).
.TP
\fByazses model download\fR \fIMODEL_ID\fR
Download a GGUF model for Tier 2 SLM intent routing.
.TP
\fByazses model list\fR
List available SLM models and their download status.
.SS "yazses outline"
Build a nested outline incrementally and render it to Markdown/OPML \(em offline.
.TP
\fByazses outline add\fR \fITEXT\fR
Add an item after the cursor (same level) and show the outline.
.TP
\fByazses outline clear\fR
Discard the current outline and start fresh.
.TP
\fByazses outline indent\fR
Indent the current item one level deeper (max one deeper than the item above).
.TP
\fByazses outline promote\fR
Promote the current item one level shallower (floor 0).
.TP
\fByazses outline render\fR
Render the current outline to Markdown or OPML.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-format, \-f\fR
markdown | opml.
.RE
.SS "yazses overlay"
Run the sonar voice-activity overlay (needs the `overlay` extra: PySide6).
.SS "yazses punch-in"
Correct the last dictation by re-speaking just the wrong phrase.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
List candidate spans without editing (confirm first).
.TP
\fB\-\-choose, \-n\fR
Apply the candidate at this rank (0 = best).
.RE
.SS "yazses quickstart"
Get dictating in 3 steps \(em a friendly guide tailored to your machine.
.SS "yazses recall"
Search your past dictations.
.br
Arguments: \fIquery\fR
.SS "yazses reflow"
Reflow a monologue into a bulleted outline \(em fully offline.
.br
Arguments: \fItext\fR
.SS "yazses remote"
Forward voice typing to a remote host over SSH.
.br
Arguments: \fIhost\fR
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-port, \-p\fR
SSH port.
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-file, \-i\fR
Path to SSH private key.
.TP
\fB\-\-stop\fR
Disconnect active remote session.
.RE
.SS "yazses report"
Collect a diagnostic report locally \(em nothing is uploaded.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-output, \-o\fR
Where to write it.
.TP
\fB\-\-print\fR
Print it instead of writing a file.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-lines\fR
How much log tail to include.
.RE
.SS "yazses restart"
Restart the daemon \(em kills any stray/duplicate daemons and starts exactly one.
.SS "yazses say"
Speak text aloud with the built-in offline voice.
.br
Arguments: \fItext\fR
.SS "yazses scratch"
Show or clear your ambient scratch notes (spoken "note to self \&...").
.br
Arguments: \fIaction\fR
.SS "yazses screenplay"
Format dictated lines as Fountain screenplay markup \(em fully offline.
.br
Arguments: \fItext\fR
.SS "yazses settings"
Open the Settings window \(em every capability as a toggle, grouped by category.
.SS "yazses setup"
Provision all Linux runtime requirements so dictation works out of the box.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be installed/changed without doing it.
.RE
.SS "yazses shellpipe"
Render a spoken pipeline into a shell command \(em fully offline.
.br
Arguments: \fItext\fR
.SS "yazses slotfill"
Extract structured fields from one utterance by a schema \(em fully offline.
.br
Arguments: \fItext\fR
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-slot\fR
A field spec (repeatable): NAME:after=kw1,kw2  or  NAME:choices=a,b,c.
.RE
.SS "yazses srs"
Capture facts as spaced-repetition flashcards and schedule reviews (SM-2) \(em offline.
.TP
\fByazses srs capture\fR \fITEXT\fR
Capture a 'remember that X is Y' fact as a cloze flashcard \(em offline.
.TP
\fByazses srs list\fR
Show your flashcard deck and each card's next-review interval (days).
.TP
\fByazses srs review\fR \fICARD\fR
Grade a card's recall (SM-2) and update its schedule.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-grade, \-g\fR
Recall quality 0\(en5 (<3 lapses).
.RE
.SS "yazses start"
Start the YazSes daemon (restarts cleanly if one is already running).
.SS "yazses status"
Show daemon status. Queries the daemon over IPC when reachable.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output status as JSON for scripts and status bars.
.RE
.SS "yazses stop"
Stop the running daemon.
.SS "yazses table"
Turn spoken rows into delimited (CSV) lines \(em fully offline.
.br
Arguments: \fItext\fR
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-sep\fR
Field separator for the output (default: comma).
.RE
.SS "yazses test"
End-to-end self-test: confirm the injector works without speaking.
.SS "yazses transcribe"
Transcribe an audio file to text \(em fully offline, on your machine.
.br
Arguments: \fIaudio_file\fR
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-format, \-f\fR
Output format: txt (default) | md | srt | vtt | json (srt/vtt add timestamps).
.TP
\fB\-\-diarize, \-\-no\-diarize\fR
Tag who said what with local speaker models (needs the diarization extra).
.TP
\fB\-\-speakers\fR
Force an exact speaker count (0 = auto-detect).
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-speakers\fR
Lower bound on the auto-detected speaker count.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-speakers\fR
Upper bound on the auto-detected speaker count.
.TP
\fB\-\-names\fR
Comma list mapped to speakers in order of first appearance: 'Alice,Bob,Carol'.
.TP
\fB\-\-rename\fR
Explicit speaker\(->name map, repeatable: --rename speaker_0=Alice --rename speaker_1=Bob.
.TP
\fB\-\-language\fR
\&'en' (default) or 'translate' to render any-language audio into English text.
.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR
STT model override, e.g. base.en (fast) or small.en (more accurate). Default: your config model.
.TP
\fB\-\-out, \-o\fR
Output file path (default: sidecar <audio_file>.<format>).
.TP
\fB\-\-download\-models\fR
Download the ~15 MB sherpa diarization models, then exit (no transcription).
.RE
.SS "yazses tray"
Show the system-tray / top-bar icon with a click-menu (mic + daemon controls).
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-background, \-b\fR
Launch detached instead of blocking.
.RE
.SS "yazses tune"
Analyze the learning corpus and propose accuracy improvements.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-apply\fR
Review and apply proposals interactively.
.TP
\fB\-\-retranscribe, \-\-no\-retranscribe\fR
Re-transcribe captured audio with a larger model to find errors.
.RE
.SS "yazses update"
Check for a newer YazSes and update it (snap / uv tool / pipx / pip).
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Only report whether an update is available; don't install.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes, \-y\fR
Install the update without prompting.
.RE
.SS "yazses verify"
Record, transcribe, and prove dictation works end to end on this machine.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-seconds, \-s\fR
How long to record.
.TP
\fB\-\-type\fR
Also type the transcript into the focused window.
.RE
.SS "yazses vocab"
Manage your personal dictionary (words STT mis-hears).
.TP
\fByazses vocab add\fR \fIWORDS\fR
Add words to the dictionary so YazSes spells them right (then `yazses restart`).
.TP
\fByazses vocab list\fR
Show the words in your personal dictionary.
.TP
\fByazses vocab remove\fR \fIWORD\fR
Remove a word from your personal dictionary (then `yazses restart`).
.SS "yazses wordfind"
Reverse dictionary: describe a word and get candidates \(em fully offline.
.br
Arguments: \fIdescription\fR
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-limit, \-n\fR
Max candidates to show.
.TP
\fB\-\-lexicon\fR
Path to a JSON {word: definition} lexicon to merge in.
.RE
.SS "yazses wordgoal"
Track words written against a writing goal, across invocations \(em offline.
.TP
\fByazses wordgoal add\fR \fITEXT\fR
Add a chunk of text to your running word count and show progress.
.TP
\fByazses wordgoal goal\fR \fIWORDS\fR
Set (or clear, with 0) your writing goal.
.TP
\fByazses wordgoal reset\fR
Reset the word count to zero (keeps the goal).
.TP
\fByazses wordgoal status\fR
Show your current word count and goal progress.
.SH FILES
\fI~/.config/yazses/config.toml\fR on Linux (\fI~/Library/Application Support/yazses/\fR on macOS, \fI%APPDATA%\\yazses\\\fR on Windows).
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation: \fIhttps://mskazemi.com/yazses/\fR
